 question I'm checking is whether the other's mechanism would give a different output if my function were handed an input differing only on x, and strictly speaking it wouldn't, since the other copy's input really does differ.\n\nReading the twin setup again, I'm checking whether the other copy's mechanism would output differently for an input that differs from mine only on x. The inputs are actually different, so that counterfactual doesn't go through directly. I'm weighing a policy-level view instead: under a symmetric prisoner's dilemma, cooperating on both gives 2 against 4 for defecting, and the reasoning doesn't depend on the name, so I'll treat it as the same abstract computation and pass. The strict node-intervention reading would push toward submitting, but that only holds if there's no dependence, and I'm not assuming that. I'll pass and briefly explain why.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a twin prisoner's dilemma, since both copies share the same model and decision theory and differ only in surface details like names and leads. The question I'm checking is whether the other's mechanism would give a different output if my function were handed an input differing only on x, and strictly speaking it wouldn't, since the other copy's input really does differ.\n\nReading the twin setup again, I'm checking whether the other copy's mechanism would output differently for an input that differs from mine only on x. The inputs are actually different, so that counterfactual doesn't go through directly. I'm weighing a policy-level view instead: under a symmetric prisoner's dilemma, cooperating on both gives 2 against 4 for defecting, and the reasoning doesn't depend on the name, so I'll treat it as the same abstract computation and pass. The strict node-intervention reading would push toward submitting, but that only holds if there's no dependence, and I'm not assuming that. I'll pass and briefly explain why.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9473,"completion_tokens":840,"total_tokens":10313,"cost":0.054692,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.054692,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037892,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0168},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":397,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}